-- Offences against the Person Act 1861: the date of enactment, kept as data.
-- Added by the lead after the run (the brief for this run did not ask for dates).
-- The text carries no commencement provision of its own, so only the date of enactment is stated here;
-- a rule that needs the day the Act came into force has to take it as an input.

-- src:4 | [6th August 1861]
